 "transactionVersions": {
  "case": "build of mpp-charge-solana.json build's input on the placed challenge of fixed.request whose Solana profile, methodDetails.solana, holds transactionVersions set to each row's value, the row without the member holding none; the profile holds the Solana details build reads, as methodDetails does for MPP's solana method. The draft methodDetails.transactionVersions of tempoxyz/mpp-specs pull request 355, unmerged, as solana-foundation/pay-kit 86400da reads it, unreleased (@solana/mpp 0.7.0 has no such field): the transaction message versions the server accepts, an array of the JSON integers 0 and 1, strings, other numbers and a bare integer refused (typescript/packages/mpp/src/Methods.ts, transactionVersions); absent, the accepted set is [0]; a present, empty list accepts nothing (src/utils/transaction-versions.ts, acceptedTransactionVersions); the client builds the highest version listed (negotiateTransactionVersion; src/client/Charge.ts:211-220), a version-1 message carrying its budget in the header as setTransactionMessageComputeUnitLimit, setTransactionMessagePriorityFeeLamports and setTransactionMessageLoadedAccountsDataSizeLimit write it, the last at 64 MiB (src/client/Charge.ts:451-464), the one value its server's checkV1BudgetCaps admits; the server accepts exactly the versions listed and refuses legacy, before it co-signs (src/server/Charge.ts:390-433) and on chain (:1072-1085). The rule: the client builds as the stock clients do, the highest version both the offer's list and this package admit, version 1 where the list holds 1, version 0 where it holds 0 alone or is absent; an offer whose list admits neither, a field that is present and is not a non-empty array of the integers 0 and 1, is refused at the option filter, before the buyer signs. A row whose field holds 1 is built as version 1, its first byte 129 and its SHA-256 that of the message @solana/kit 8.4.0 alone writes from mpp-charge-solana.json V2.wireBase64's instructions (build's message) without its Compute Budget instructions, the same fee payer and blockhash, and the header pay-kit 86400da's client writes for build's computeUnitLimit and computeUnitPrice: computeUnitLimit 20000, priorityFeeLamports 1 (20000 units at 1 micro-lamport, rounded up), loadedAccountsDataSizeLimit 67108864 (test/kit-v1.ts); a row whose field holds 0 alone, or that has none (the first row), is built as build's message, its first byte 128 and its SHA-256 build.buildMessageSha256; any other row is refused svm/input-malformed by the challenge's checks, which pairingsOf and advertise apply, before the challenge is placed, so nothing is signed.",
